Description: pass the help text as a printf argument
 main() called printf(sHelp) with the string used directly as the format
 string; Debian's -Werror=format-security (injected by dh) rejects that,
 and any '%' in the translated text would have been interpreted as a
 conversion. Use printf("%s", sHelp).
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Moe
--- a/source/MoeApplication.cpp
+++ b/source/MoeApplication.cpp
@@ -328,7 +328,7 @@
 main(int argc, char **argv)
 {
   if (argc == 1)
-    printf(sHelp);
+    printf("%s", sHelp);
 
   MoeApplication().Run();
 }
